# Grim Hollow Player's Guide 2024 Transformations: Shadowsteel Ghoul, Specter, Vampire, plus the Gifts of Dread.
TRANS = {
 "Shadowsteel Ghoul": {
  "intro": "Shadowsteel is a vile metal that soaks up corrupt power, and casters who use it for curses bind their soul to it a little at a time. Casting with a Shadowsteel Spellcasting Focus, attuning to a Shadowsteel item, or carrying a Shadowsteel weapon for long enough can start the curse. Once you reach Stage 1, only a Wish level effect can lift it. Each stage needs a story event, such as casting a curse on a powerful foe, consuming a Shadowsteel item in a ritual, or failing two Death Saving Throws.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 1 Boon and gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Shadowsteel Ghoul stage 1. Pick Shadowsteel Curser or Shadowsteel Weapon, and lose 2 points in one ability score."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose two Stage 2 Boons and gain the Stage 2 Flaw. Shadowsteel Caster needs Shadowsteel Curser, and Shadowsteel Weapon Master needs Shadowsteel Weapon.", "take": 2, "fixed": [], "d": "Shadowsteel Ghoul stage 2. Pick two Boons such as Magic Resistance or Shadowsteel Caster, and become Friendless."},
   3: {"rule": "Gain the Cursed Claw Boon and the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 0, "fixed": ["Cursed Claw"], "d": "Shadowsteel Ghoul stage 3. Gain the Cursed Claw attack, but you heal at half rate."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon and gain the Stage 4 Flaw. Shadowsteel Arcane Vessel needs Shadowsteel Caster.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Shadowsteel Ghoul stage 4. Pick Shadowsteel Arcane Vessel or Shadowsteel Fury, and risk a Shadowsteel Explosion."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Shadowsteel Curser": "You gain the Shadowsteel Adept feat if you do not have it. When you cast a Shadowsteel curse, its casting time is halved and its saving throw DC rises by 1.",
   "Shadowsteel Weapon": "During a Long Rest you imbue one Melee weapon within reach with a fragment of your corruption. It counts as magical. When you reduce a creature to 0 Hit Points with a melee attack using it, you gain 1d8 Temporary Hit Points for 1 hour. Imbuing a new weapon removes the effect from the old one.",
   "Debilitating Magic": "Choose one ability score. You lose 2 points in it as the Shadowsteel eats at your body, soul, or both.",
   "Magic Resistance": "You have Advantage on saving throws against spells.",
   "Shadowsteel Absorption": "The Shadowsteel hardens your flesh. Your Armor Class increases by 1 while you wear no armor.",
   "Shadowsteel Caster": "Requires Shadowsteel Curser. You gain the Shadowsteel Master feat if you do not have it. When you cast a spell with a spell slot using a Shadowsteel component, you can spend a Hit Die to regain that slot. The slot level cannot exceed twice your Transformation Stage. You can do this a number of times equal to your spellcasting ability modifier, and you regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Shadowsteel Weapon Master": "Requires Shadowsteel Weapon. You gain a +4 bonus to damage rolls made with your Shadowsteel Weapon.",
   "Friendless": "You can no longer connect with others socially. You cannot count as an ally to any Humanoid or Beast, no living creature can be Friendly toward you, and you have Disadvantage on all Charisma ability checks.",
   "Cursed Claw": "You gain a Claw attack that uses Strength or Dexterity for attack and damage. You can make it twice with the Attack action or once as a Bonus Action. It deals 2d6 plus the ability modifier. On a hit the target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or gain a random Shadowsteel curse at Stage 1. The DC is 8 plus your Constitution modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. A creature that already has a Shadowsteel curse is not affected.",
   "Healing Resistance": "Whenever you regain Hit Points, from magic or natural means, you regain only half as many as normal. You still recover all Hit Points at the end of a Long Rest.",
   "Shadowsteel Arcane Vessel": "Requires Shadowsteel Caster. When you cast a spell with a spell slot, one creature targeted by it within 60 feet has Disadvantage on the saving throw, or you have Advantage on the spell attack roll. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Shadowsteel Fury": "When you take the Attack action with your Shadowsteel Weapon or Cursed Claw, you can use a Bonus Action to attack again with the same weapon or claw. On a hit the target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or gain 1 Exhaustion level. The DC is 8 plus the ability modifier you used plus your Transformation Stage.",
   "Shadowsteel Explosion": "The first time you are Bloodied or drop to 0 Hit Points after finishing a Short Rest or Long Rest, the Shadowsteel in your flesh lashes out. All living creatures within 60 feet must make a DC 20 Constitution saving throw. A failure means 4d10 Force damage and the Stunned condition until the end of their next turn. A success means half damage and no Stun.",
  },
 },
 "Specter": {
  "intro": "A Specter is a living creature whose ties to the material world are being torn away by death, contact with the realm of the dead, or the chaos of the Aether Kindred. From Stage 1 on, ordinary magic such as Remove Curse cannot end it, and nothing weaker than Wish can revive or restore you while the spirit is anchored. Once you die completely and your soul departs, normal resurrection magic can bring you back free of the Transformation. Each stage needs a story event, such as defeating a ghostly Undead, surviving a Hit Point maximum drain, or opening a path to the realm of the dead.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "Gain the Spectral Form Boon, choose one other Stage 1 Boon, and gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Spectral Form"], "d": "Specter stage 1. Become Undead as well, pick Ghastly Touch or Incorporeal Movement, and suffer Disadvantage on Death Saving Throws."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon and gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Specter stage 2. Pick Ethereal Phasing or Haunting Flight, and heal at half rate."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon and gain the Stage 3 Flaw. Draining Flight needs Incorporeal Movement and Haunting Flight, and Paralyzing Touch needs Ghastly Touch.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Specter stage 3. Pick Draining Flight or Paralyzing Touch, and risk Confusion when first Bloodied."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon and gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Specter stage 4. Pick Call of Unmaking or Possession, and take force damage when you roll a natural 1."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Spectral Form": "You count as Undead in addition to your other creature types and cannot be excluded from Turn Undead. You have Resistance to Necrotic damage, or Immunity if you already had that Resistance. You stop aging, ignore any effect that would age you, and cannot die of old age.",
   "Ghastly Touch": "Once per turn, when you hit a target within 5 feet with a melee attack, you can deal an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage. You can do this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage, and regain all uses after a Short Rest or Long Rest.",
   "Incorporeal Movement": "As a Magic action you become incorporeal until the start of your next turn. You can move through solid objects at full Speed, but take 1d10 Force damage if you end your turn inside one and are moved to the nearest open space. You have Resistance to all damage except Force and you are Lightly Obscured. You can use this a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Drawn to Darkness": "Your life force is pulled toward oblivion. You have Disadvantage on Death Saving Throws.",
   "Ethereal Phasing": "You can cast Blink without a spell slot a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage, regaining all uses after a Long Rest. While Blink cast this way is active, you gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage at the start of each of your turns.",
   "Haunting Flight": "You gain a Fly Speed equal to your Speed. While flying, you can use a Bonus Action to target one creature you can see within 30 feet. It must succeed on a Wisdom saving throw or be Frightened for 1 minute. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. You must finish a Short Rest or Long Rest before using this again.",
   "Untethered from Life": "Your life force is frail. Whenever you regain Hit Points, you regain only half as many, rounded down.",
   "Draining Flight": "Requires Incorporeal Movement and Haunting Flight. You can use Incorporeal Movement as a Bonus Action, and your Fly Speed from Haunting Flight becomes double your Speed. While incorporeal, your movement does not provoke Opportunity Attacks and you can damage creatures you pass through. Once per turn, when you enter a creature's space, it must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take 6d6 Psychic damage and be Frightened until the end of your next turn. A success halves the damage and avoids the Fright. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. You must finish a Short Rest or Long Rest before using this again.",
   "Paralyzing Touch": "Requires Ghastly Touch. Its damage becomes 2d6 Necrotic. Any creature you damage with it must make a Constitution saving throw against a DC of 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. On a failure it is Paralyzed until the start of your next turn, and on a success it is Prone instead. You can do this a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage, regaining all uses after a Short Rest or Long Rest.",
   "Fraying Reality": "The first time you become Bloodied after finishing a Short Rest or Long Rest, you must make a DC 15 Charisma saving throw. On a failure you act as if under the Confusion spell for 1 minute.",
   "Call of Unmaking": "As a Bonus Action you wail, and all creatures of your choice within 30 feet, except Constructs and Undead, must make a Constitution saving throw. Creatures that cannot hear you have Advantage. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage. On a failure the creature bears the Mark of Unmaking for 1 minute and takes an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage each time it takes damage. You can use this once, then you need a Long Rest.",
   "Possession": "As a Magic action you enter the space of a Humanoid or Beast, which must make a DC 15 Charisma saving throw. On a failure you vanish into it, it is Incapacitated, and you control its body while it stays aware. You cannot be targeted while possessing. You keep your alignment, Intelligence, Wisdom, Charisma, and your Charmed and Frightened immunities, and otherwise use the host's statistics without its knowledge, spells, class features, or proficiencies. It lasts 1 hour, until the host drops to 0 Hit Points, until you end it as a Bonus Action, or until an effect forces you out. You then appear within 5 feet of the host. You must finish a Short Rest or Long Rest before using this again.",
   "Pull of Oblivion": "When you roll a natural 1 on a D20 Test, you take 4d6 Force damage that nothing can reduce. If it drops you to 0 Hit Points you die. When you die in this or any other way, only magic equal to a 7th-level or higher spell can bring you back.",
  },
 },
 "Vampire": {
  "intro": "A Vampire is born when a mortal contracts the Sanguine Curse, dies, and rises undead, through a Vampire's blood, its bite, dark magic, or cursed artifacts. Talk with your GM about what kind of Vampire you become. From Stage 1 on, only Wish level magic can cure it. Each stage needs a story event, such as severing a tie to your mortal life, drinking the blood of an older Vampire, failing two Death Saving Throws, or performing a Sangromancy blood ritual. You must also feed on about 1 pint of mortal blood at the interval your Flaw demands. As an action you can bite a living creature within 5 feet that is Charmed by you or is Incapacitated, Paralyzed, Restrained, or Unconscious. It loses a pint of blood and gains 1 Exhaustion level. If you miss your feeding window you enter a feeding frenzy under GM control until you drain a creature dry, and then you fall unconscious for 4 hours.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "Gain the Fanged Bite Boon, choose one bloodline Boon, and gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Fanged Bite"], "d": "Vampire stage 1. Gain Fanged Bite and a Soman, Strigoi, or Fzeg bloodline, and fall under the Sanguine Curse."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose two Stage 2 Boons and gain the Stage 2 Flaw, which replaces the Stage 1 Flaw's feeding interval with a shorter one.", "take": 2, "fixed": [], "d": "Vampire stage 2. Pick two Boons such as Undead Resilience, and take Disadvantage in sunlight."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose two Stage 3 Boons and gain the Stage 3 Flaw. Sangromancy Specialist needs a spellcaster who can cast cantrips.", "take": 2, "fixed": [], "d": "Vampire stage 3. Pick two Boons such as Mist Form or Improved Fanged Bite, and burn in sunlight."},
   4: {"rule": "Gain the Regeneration Boon, choose one Final bloodline Boon that matches your Stage 1 bloodline, and gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Regeneration"], "d": "Vampire stage 4. Gain Regeneration and your Final bloodline, but a stake or silver crit can destroy you."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Fanged Bite": "As an Attack action you can make a Bite attack, using Strength or Dexterity, and you are proficient with it. It deals 1d6 plus the ability modifier Piercing damage and is neither a weapon nor an Unarmed Strike. If it hits a creature that has blood, the target must succeed on a Constitution saving throw or take an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage, and you regain Hit Points equal to that Necrotic damage. The DC is 8 plus your Proficiency Bonus plus your Transformation Stage.",
   "Soman Bloodline": "The most common bloodline in Etharis. Your Strength and Dexterity each increase by 1, to a maximum of 19. You have Advantage on attack rolls with Fanged Bite, its Necrotic damage becomes 1d8, and you gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed.",
   "Strigoi Bloodline": "Your Dexterity increases by 2, to a maximum of 20. If you make Fanged Bite with Advantage, its Piercing damage becomes 2d4 plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. You can take the Hide action as a Bonus Action and can Hide anywhere out of sunlight. You gain Stealth proficiency, or Expertise in Stealth if you were already proficient.",
   "Fzeg Bloodline": "A bloodline that mixes vampirism with lycanthropy. Your Strength increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, and your Speed increases by 10 feet. You gain a Claw attack that deals 1d8 plus your Strength modifier Slashing damage, using Strength and your Proficiency Bonus for the attack, and it is neither a weapon nor an Unarmed Strike. When you make the Claw attack with the Attack action, you can use a Bonus Action to make a Fanged Bite attack.",
   "The Sanguine Curse": "You cannot enter a private residence you do not own unless an occupant invites you, and the invitation holds while the inviter lives there. If you enter uninvited you have Disadvantage on all D20 Tests there, take 1d4 Psychic damage at the start of each of your turns, and cannot have Resistance or Immunity to Psychic damage there. You must feed at least once every seven days.",
   "Eyes of the Night": "You gain Darkvision out to 60 feet. If you already have Darkvision, its range increases by 60 feet.",
   "Grave-Touched Soul": "You gain Resistance to Necrotic damage, or Immunity if you already had that Resistance.",
   "Inhuman Reflexes": "You have Advantage on Dexterity saving throws.",
   "Undead Resilience": "When any damage except Radiant would reduce you to 0 Hit Points, you can drop to 1 Hit Point instead. You can use this once, then you need a Long Rest.",
   "Greater Sanguine Curse": "You have Disadvantage on all D20 Tests while in sunlight. You must feed every 4 days.",
   "Beguiler's Charm": "As a Magic action, choose a Humanoid or Beast within 30 feet that can see you. It must succeed on a Charisma saving throw against a DC of 8 plus your Charisma modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus or be Charmed for 24 hours. When the 24 hours end you can renew the Charm with no save. You can hold only one creature this way, and the Charm ends early if you target another or if you or an ally damages the creature.",
   "Improved Fanged Bite": "You can make 2 Fanged Bite attacks with the Attack action. You can also make a Fanged Bite as a Bonus Action on a turn when you did not bite as part of the Attack action.",
   "Mist Form": "You can cast Gaseous Form without a spell slot or components a number of times equal to your Vampire Transformation Stage, and regain all uses after a Long Rest. You can cast it as an action, or as a Reaction when you would take Bludgeoning, Piercing, or Slashing damage, before the damage lands.",
   "Sangromancy Specialist": "You gain an extra 1d12 Sangromancy Hit Die per Vampire Transformation Stage, usable on Sangromancy spells, and you regain spent ones after a Long Rest. When Fanged Bite restores Hit Points to you, you regain one spent Sangromancy Die. Any Necrotic cantrip you cast can be boosted by spending up to 2 Hit Dice, Sangromancy Dice included, for extra Necrotic damage, decided after you know whether the cantrip affects its targets.",
   "Supreme Sanguine Curse": "If you start your turn in sunlight you take 1d10 Radiant damage, and nothing can give you Resistance or Immunity to it. You must feed every 2 days. In stressful moments your true appearance shows against your will, and you can otherwise hide it by concentrating on your composure. Triggers include becoming Bloodied, concentrating on a spell, taking sunlight damage, a feeding frenzy, being Unconscious, entering hallowed ground, or choosing to reveal yourself. In these cases and other extreme stress the GM can call for a Constitution saving throw (DC 16 at Stage 3, DC 20 at Stage 4), and on a failure your curse is revealed. Non-evil creatures who see your true form turn Hostile unless the GM decides otherwise.",
   "Final Soman Bloodline": "Requires Soman Bloodline. Your Strength and Dexterity each increase by 1, to a maximum of 20, and the Necrotic damage of Fanged Bite becomes 3d8. A Humanoid reduced to 0 Hit Points by your Fanged Bite or your feeding rises as a Vampire Spawn 24 hours later unless the body is destroyed or warded by ritual. You can control two such Spawn that obey your spoken commands. Taking a third releases one of the others.",
   "Final Strigoi Bloodline": "Requires Strigoi Bloodline. Your Dexterity increases by 2, to a maximum of 20. As a Bonus Action you can summon 2d4 Swarms of Rats, Swarms of Bats, or Wolves, which appear at the start of your next turn within 60 feet and obey your verbal or mental commands. They vanish after 1 hour, when you drop to 0 Hit Points, or when you dismiss them as a Bonus Action. You regain this after a Short Rest or Long Rest. You can also cast Misty Step up to four times without a slot, even as a Reaction when a weapon attack targets you, before damage. You regain these casts after a Long Rest.",
   "Final Fzeg Bloodline": "Requires Fzeg Bloodline. Your Strength increases by 2, to a maximum of 20, and your Speed increases by 10 feet. Your Claw deals 3d6 plus your Strength modifier Slashing damage, and you can make three Claw attacks with the Attack action. You have Resistance to Bludgeoning, Piercing, and Slashing damage, which magic and silvered weapons ignore.",
   "Regeneration": "At the start of your turn you regain 15 Hit Points if you have at least 1 but fewer than 60 Hit Points. This does nothing while you are in sunlight or if you took Radiant damage since the end of your last turn.",
   "Ultimate Sanguine Curse": "When you are Incapacitated, Stunned, or Unconscious and take a Critical Hit from a Piercing weapon made of wood or silver, you must succeed on a DC 20 Constitution saving throw or die and crumble to ash. Only True Resurrection or Wish can bring you back. You must feed every day.",
  },
 },
}

GIFT_D = "Pick one Gift of Dread, a bargain boon from a Fiend contract that each stage of the Transformation can unlock."

GIFT_INTRO = "A Gift of Dread is a boon the daemonic powers grant you when you sign a contract that gives a willing mortal Humanoid their desired wish. The contract needs magical ink and paper worth 10 GP per Transformation Stage you have reached, and you cannot benefit from the mortal's wish. You can only take a gift of your current stage or lower, and only one gift is active at a time. After a Long Rest you can swap to any gift from a contract you have signed."

GIFTS = {
 "Gift of Joyous Life": "At the start of your turn while you are Bloodied, you can roll a Hit Point Die (no action) and regain Hit Points equal to the roll. On a 1 you regain nothing and take 1 Force damage. You regain this after a Short Rest or Long Rest.",
 "Gift of Liberating Freedom": "While not wearing Heavy armor, you can use a Bonus Action to manifest leathery wings that give you a Fly Speed equal to half your Speed. They vanish if you dismiss them as a Bonus Action, fall Unconscious, or become Bloodied. You can keep them out for 1 hour in total, across several stints, and regain that hour after a Long Rest.",
 "Gift of Martial Prowess": "Once per turn, when you miss with a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, you can reroll it. On a hit you spend 3 Hit Dice and add the total as Force damage. On a miss you spend 3 Hit Dice and take Psychic damage equal to the total. You need at least 3 Hit Dice to use this, and after a rerolled attack hits you cannot use it again until a Long Rest.",
 "Gift of Prodigious Talent": "Choose two skills and gain Expertise in them. If you roll a 1 or 2 on an ability check with either skill, you lose half your maximum Hit Dice, rounded down, and do not regain them until you finish two Long Rests.",
 "Gift of Second Chances": "When you drop to 0 Hit Points, you can use your Reaction to roll a Hit Die. On a 2 or higher, your Hit Points become the result. Otherwise you suffer a Death Saving Throw failure. You regain this after a Long Rest.",
 "Gift of Unbridled Power": "After a Short Rest you can spend 2 Hit Dice and regain spell slot levels equal to the highest number rolled, but you take Psychic damage equal to twice the total rolled. You regain this after a Long Rest.",
 "Gift of Unconditional Love": "When a creature you can see within 30 feet fails a saving throw, you can use your Reaction to gain Temporary Hit Points equal to 1d10 plus your Transformation Stage. On a 1 you gain none and fall Prone. You regain this after a Short Rest or Long Rest.",
 "Gift of Unfettered Glory": "When you damage a creature with a melee attack, an Unarmed Strike, or a cantrip, you deal an extra 2 Force damage per Transformation Stage. Each Hit Die you roll to heal during a Short Rest restores 2 fewer Hit Points.",
 "Gift of Unsurpassed Fortune": "When an enemy you can see within 10 feet succeeds on an attack roll or saving throw, you can use your Reaction to roll a d20. On a 6 or higher the attack misses or the save fails, and you regain your Reaction. Otherwise you take 1d6 Psychic damage per Transformation Stage that nothing can reduce. You regain this after a Long Rest.",
}
